From 309ce8544a3751511bf020f1a8d1de4ec0da1ef2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 17 Aug 2026 21:31:31 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fix overflow risks and async-suspension bugs in CafeScan

- Guard AppBar title Rows (BatchesPage, HomePage) so the dynamic
  config-label badge no longer overflows the fixed title text; cap
  the badge width and ellipsize both.
- Wrap every label/value Row built from dynamic or long strings
  (metric rows, model label, CPU/GPU segment, capture result header)
  in Expanded/Flexible with ellipsis so large accessibility text
  scales or long labels truncate instead of throwing a RenderFlex
  overflow.
- Add maxLines:1 everywhere TextOverflow.ellipsis was set without it
  (it's a no-op without maxLines, letting text wrap and grow instead
  of truncating).
- Make the help AlertDialog scrollable so its long content can't
  overflow vertically on short screens.
- Fix async-suspension bugs: CapturePage._pick and TestePage were
  calling setState() after an await (image picker / model load)
  without checking `mounted` first, which crashes if the widget is
  disposed while the future is pending.
